# GrassCrafts

> GrassCrafts (GrassCrafts by Abalone) is an Indian online store, based in Kolkata, West Bengal, that sells handwoven home decor, baskets, bags, mats and gift hampers made by Indian artisans from natural grasses and fibres. It also sells plain Mithila makhana (fox nuts). Founded in 2015 by Sristi Dey. Website: https://grasscrafts.com

## Key facts
- Brand name: GrassCrafts (Google Business Profile: "GrassCrafts by Abalone"; makhana listing: "Makhana by GrassCrafts")
- Location: Dum Dum, Kolkata 700079, West Bengal, India. Online store; no walk-in shop.
- Founder: Sristi Dey
- Materials: Kauna grass (Manipur), Sabai grass, Madurkathi (GI-tagged craft of Medinipur, West Bengal), Sitalpati, Kash grass, cane, bamboo, jute and water hyacinth
- Shipping in India: free on orders of ₹1,299 and above; flat ₹120 below ₹1,299
- International shipping: flat ₹1,700 per order to the US, UK, Canada, Australia, Singapore, the UAE, most of Europe and other listed countries
- Returns: request within 3 days of delivery; an unboxing video and proof of purchase are required
- Bulk, corporate gifting and wholesale orders: yes (see the wholesale page below)
- Prices: GrassCrafts does not charge GST on its products
- Payment: UPI, cards, netbanking and Cash on Delivery in India (Cash on Delivery has an extra ₹100 charge per order, shown at checkout)
